Keep the soft TLB and the jump cache of up to 8 x86 PCIDs across CR3 writes in QEMU's TCG.

Research prototype for kaeawc/simee#227, not for upstream as it stands (see
docs/research/tcg-context-switch.md): no INVPCID, no CR4.PCIDE checks beyond what TCG did,
x86 only, and the measured gain on a whole guest boot is within noise.

Applies to the QEMU 11.1.3 release tarball (sha256 5a8289c7940dc77d... as in
docs/research/software-mode-profile.md):

    tar xf qemu-11.1.3.tar.xz && cd qemu-11.1.3 && patch -p1 < tcg-pcid.patch

Run emu with EMU_QEMU pointing at the qemu-system-x86_64 built from the patched tree. The guest then
sees CPUID.PCID and its kernel sets CR4.PCIDE; `info jit` in the monitor gains "TLB PCID
switches" and "TLB PCID bank hits".

